### What are common mistakes?

Common mistakes include off-by-one errors, not handling edge cases like empty input, and not considering the constraints of the problem.

### What are the edge cases?

Edge cases include empty input, single element input, all identical elements, and boundary values.

### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer should understand the time-space tradeoffs, be able to explain the algorithm clearly, and know when this technique applies versus alternatives.
